    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "p1",
      "x": 100,
      "y": 770,
      "width": 960,
      "height": 21.75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#d0384a",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 13081,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 13081,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783762000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14.5,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "L, A, and B are bit-identical across the two worlds — so ANY merge function produces the same bottom state in both.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 11.600000000000001,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "L, A, and B are bit-identical across the two worlds — so ANY merge function produces the same bottom state in both.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b1C",
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "p2",
      "x": 100,
      "y": 802,
      "width": 745.0783081054688,
      "height": 46.875,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#5b6575",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 13082,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1407947294,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783764628800,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 12.5,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "But the required outputs differ. Hence no merge over these states is order-faithful: the p-vs-k order was decided at\ninsertion time by g₁’s timestamp, and after the splices no state contains it. (The ts-rule k·10 > p·5 picks world 2’s answer\n— fooled in world 1.) Bounded per-node state ⇒ some dead rank is forgotten ⇒ some pair of worlds collides.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 10,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "But the required outputs differ. Hence no merge over these states is order-faithful: the p-vs-k order was decided at\ninsertion time by g₁’s timestamp, and after the splices no state contains it. (The ts-rule k·10 > p·5 picks world 2’s answer\n— fooled in world 1.) Bounded per-node state ⇒ some dead rank is forgotten ⇒ some pair of worlds collides.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b1D",
      "autoResize": true
    },
